  T('sx-d4-wrap', 'Domain 4 shift: a malicious macro', 'Security operations in one incident',
    'Incident: the macro from 4.9 ran on PC-0331. Work it end to end. PowerShell (domain admin rights, EDR module). Each task names its objective.',
    { shell: 'ps', prompt: 'PS C:\\IR>' },
    [{ t: '<b>4.8</b> — Containment: isolate PC-0331 with the EDR vendor\'s PowerShell module (simulated cmdlet for this lab: Invoke-EdrIsolation -ComputerName). In Microsoft Defender this is the "Isolate device" action.', accept: [/^invoke-edrisolation -computername pc-0331$/i], show: 'Invoke-EdrIsolation -ComputerName PC-0331', hint: '4.8 — Invoke-EdrIsolation -ComputerName <host>', out: 'PC-0331 isolated (EDR channel only).', why: 'Stop the spread while keeping the evidence.' },
     { t: '<b>4.6</b> — Disable the user\'s account (lmorgan) until the password is reset and sessions revoked.', accept: [/^disable-adaccount( -identity)? lmorgan$/i], show: 'Disable-ADAccount -Identity lmorgan', hint: '4.6 — Disable-ADAccount', out: '', why: 'Contain the identity as well as the host.' },
     { t: '<b>4.9</b> — Hunt: check the DNS log for any other host resolving cdn-update-check.xyz.', accept: [/^select-string( -path)? \.?\\?dns\.log -pattern ['"]cdn-update-check\.xyz['"]$/i, /^sls ['"]cdn-update-check\.xyz['"] \.?\\?dns\.log$/i], show: 'Select-String -Path .\\dns.log -Pattern "cdn-update-check.xyz"', hint: '4.9 — Select-String', out: 'dns.log:88213: 09:41:10 10.1.20.31 Q A cdn-update-check.xyz\ndns.log:90117: 10:02:55 10.1.20.58 Q A cdn-update-check.xyz', ask: { q: 'Which second internal IP resolved the domain?', accept: ['10.1.20.58'], why: 'A second victim — isolate it too and widen the scope.' }, why: 'Threat hunting across data sources.' },
     { t: '<b>4.5</b> — Block the domain for everyone with a DNS sinkhole entry on the DNS server (Add-DnsServerQueryResolutionPolicy is complex — use the zone method: Add-DnsServerPrimaryZone for the domain).', accept: [/^add-dnsserverprimaryzone( -name)? ['"]?cdn-update-check\.xyz['"]? -replicationscope ['"]?domain['"]?$/i, /^add-dnsserverprimaryzone -name ['"]?cdn-update-check\.xyz['"]? -replicationscope ['"]?(domain|forest)['"]?$/i], show: 'Add-DnsServerPrimaryZone -Name "cdn-update-check.xyz" -ReplicationScope "Domain"', hint: '4.5 — Add-DnsServerPrimaryZone -Name … -ReplicationScope "Domain"', out: '', why: 'An empty local zone means the domain no longer resolves internally (a simple sinkhole). Also block it at the web filter and firewall.' },
     { t: '<b>4.4</b> — Check how many alerts the new "Office spawns PowerShell" SIEM rule raised today (simulated SIEM cmdlet for this lab: Get-SiemAlert -Rule; real SIEMs use their own query language).', accept: [/^\(?get-siemalert -rule ['"]office spawns powershell['"]( -since \(get-date\)\.date)?\)?(\.count| \| measure(-object)?)$/i], show: '(Get-SiemAlert -Rule "Office spawns PowerShell" -Since (Get-Date).Date).Count', hint: '4.4 — (Get-SiemAlert -Rule "…").Count', out: '2', why: 'Both victims, no noise — a well-tuned rule. Lessons learned: block macros from the Internet by policy (4.1 baseline).' }],
    'Domain 4 in one incident: contain (4.8), identity (4.6), hunt across sources (4.9), modify capabilities (4.5), monitoring quality (4.4).',
    ['Each task names its objective.']);
